# Spec 026 AC-8, on the console: the bench (Y) runs four mono workloads of 600 frames — throughput (a textured, lit
# 12 032-triangle sphere), draws (256 cubes, 1 directional + 2 point lights), cpu (512 draws, half behind the camera, 128
# blended), fill (three full-screen blended planes over a model) — then, with the slider up (this script's `slider 1`),
# two stereo ones (026b): throughput 6000 stereo (a 6 016-triangle sphere) and draws 256 stereo. One line each:
#   3d bench: <case> avg <ms> worst <ms> missed <n>/600 rec <ms> sub <ms> prep <ms> cpu <ms>
# (per frame: rec = recording, sub = the "gfx submit" scope, prep = culling and ordering, cpu = AC-8's CPU share;
# sub and prep exist in Development builds) then the verdict against AC-8's budgets, mono and stereo (set from the
# Old 3DS XL, plan 026). Record the numbers in plan 026 whatever the verdict.
# Console: nnh run models --script examples/models/tests/bench.nnhs   (Homebrew Launcher open, press Y)
# (In the simulator the numbers mean nothing: it doesn't model the PICA200's speed.)
fail-on "] E "
fail-on "3d bench: FAIL"

wait 30
tap Y
expect "3d bench: started" 20
expect "3d bench: throughput 12000 avg" 700
expect "3d bench: draws 256 avg" 700
expect "3d bench: cpu 512 avg" 700
expect "3d bench: fill avg" 700
expect "3d bench: stereo waiting for the slider" 30
wait 10
slider 1
expect "3d bench: throughput 6000 stereo avg" 700
expect "3d bench: draws 256 stereo avg" 700
expect "3d bench: PASS" 30
wait 10
screenshot bench eyes
slider off
end
